{"about":"Redaction conformance cases, carried byte for byte by dutiona/knowledge-base and dutiona/memory-engine. Each output is one pass of memory-engine's redaction engine: redact.rs at 97c8e77 with the owner rulings of 2026-11-17 applied, then memory-engine#1024's token prefixes, its SendGrid fix (a dot in the body after SG.) its url-credential fix (the scan resumes inside an authority, so a password after a path-less URL is found) and its link fix (a link exempts only a match that starts in its body, after the scheme, so a token glued to a URL is found). The rulings: no email detector (email is not a secret); the ADR-0020 machine-token detector first; and links exempt. A link is a scheme, a colon, two slashes, then RFC 3986 characters other than the apostrophe, parentheses, comma and semicolon. Inside a link no rule matches but url-credential, which removes the password of a user:pass userinfo; the userinfo itself and machine tokens stay subject to every rule, and a private-key header line stops where a link starts. Example tokens only."}
